:''For the [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] counterpart, see [[Dark Aegis Garu (Uber Rare Cat)]].''
'''Baby Garu''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] released in [[Version 10.1 Update|Version 10.1]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] event. Similar to most other UBERFEST exclusives, Baby Garu has very different stats between forms, providing different usage in various situations.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 585
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Baby Garu
|name2 = Mighty Aegis Garu
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mighty Aegis Garu''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit is a universal tank, having more health against traited enemies than even [[Hades the Punisher (Uber Rare Cat)|Hades]], but his stats allow him to also be a dangerous offensive force, with the combination of [[Omni Strike]] (which grants forward piercing range in Evolved Form only, but worse backward reach against Zombies burrowing behind in both forms), [[Mini-Wave]] and, of course, great attack power. He can be used in most situations that do not involve many [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] or [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemies as a solid support unit, who will both defend the rest of the Cat army and provide solid damage, but he isn't a very good tank as he stands behind your attackers, serving as a second line of defense but also leaving your frontliners vulnerable to enemy fire.

Although his Normal Form suffers from a very long cooldown, due to being cheap for his purpose, he is a great unit in [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] stages, while the Evolved Form tends to perform better elsewhere. Since Mighty Aegis has Omni Strike with a piercing range, this unit is more effective when close to the enemy base due to [[Hitbox#Omni Strike unit on base|how Omni Strike interacts with bases]], and he can also hit a few more enemies when he isn't close enough. This unit can still be used as an attacker against [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies, as long as he doesn't get outranged by too many enemies in the stage you're playing. He can also serve as a counter against [[Zollow]], notoriously known for being one of the most annoying enemies, if he has enough levels to one shot them with his mini-wave.

